    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d789">

                <pb facs="1075" n="1065" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1065"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Nanking Embassy Files, Lot F79, 820 Surplus
                    Property: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Consul
                        General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-01-17T19:00:00+07:00">January 17, 1946—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. For Ploward and Johnson from General Marshall. Agree with your recommendation
                    re Calcutta stockpile. (Re Shanghai’s No. 14 of January 10.) Please advise your
                    Indian office accordingly. Question being taken up with Chinese authorities in
                    Chungking where they will be offered terms you recommend and informed that quick
                    decision necessary or otherwise trucks will be disposed of to the Philippines.
                    [Marshall.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
